From: Eduardo Ruiz <335073+eduarbo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 01:25:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the file cache on while a game list view is made

- The cache's activator sat inside the block that returns a view made
  before, so it ended before the new view was made and cached nothing. It
  now lasts until the view is made, as its comment says.
---
 es-app/src/views/ViewController.cpp | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/es-app/src/views/ViewController.cpp b/es-app/src/views/ViewController.cpp
index a5904d62..eade1b11 100644
--- a/es-app/src/views/ViewController.cpp
+++ b/es-app/src/views/ViewController.cpp
@@ -680,10 +680,14 @@ std::shared_ptr<IGameListView> ViewController::getGameListView(SystemData* syste
 
 		if (!loadIfnull)
 			return nullptr;
+	}
 
-		// The view's elements and its games' media check the same files again and again: once each
-		Utils::FileSystem::FileSystemCacheActivator fsc;
+	// The view's elements and its games' media check the same files again and again: once each, while the
+	// view is made
+	Utils::FileSystem::FileSystemCacheActivator fsc;
 
+	if (createAsPopupAndSetExitFunction == nullptr)
+	{
 		system->setUIModeFilters();
 		system->updateDisplayedGameCount();
 	}
